ats with grassland, meadows, and openings in chaparral, woodland or forest (oak, redwood, pine or fir), primarily along the coast and in the Coast Ranges, with scattered locations elsewhere.', '0', '9597', '3.98', '167.94', '<p>Prefers sun or part shade.&nbsp;</p>', null, 'By seed.  For propagating by seed:  Soak in warm water 6 hrs. ( Emery and Frey 1971).', '4', '18', '3', '6', 'Mallow, Checker', 'Wild Hollyhock,Checker Mallow,Dwarf Checkerbloom,California Checkerbloom', null, 'Common', 'N', 'https://ucjeps.berkeley.edu/eflora/eflora_display.php?name=Sidalcea+malviflora', 'https://calscape.org/Sidalcea-malviflora-%28Checker-Bloom%29', 'https://calscape.org/storage/app/media/qr/Sidalcea-malviflora-%28Checker-Bloom%29.png');
