grassy places, clearings, disturbed places, recently burned places, at moderate to high elevations', '722', '3571', '4.79', '115.66', 'Plant in sandy or loamy soils that are at least 20 inches deep, with a pH of 6.5-8.5. It is intolerant of anaerobic soils, moderately tolerant of calcareous soils, and tolerant of infertile soils. Wyethia mollis is extremely drought tolerant. It requires a minimum of 8 inches of water per year, and a maximum of 16 inches of water per year once established. It is very tolerant of shade. Prefers sun or part shade.', null, 'For propagating by seed: 3 months stratification. No treatment may give satisfactory germination.', '24', '24', '36', '36', 'Mule Ears, Wooly', 'Mountain Mule Ears,Mule-ears,Woolly Mule''s-ears,Mountain Mule-ears,Woolly Mule-ears', null, null, 'N', 'https://ucjeps.berkeley.edu/eflora/eflora_display.php?name=Wyethia+mollis', 'https://calscape.org/Wyethia-mollis-%28Mule-Ears%29', 'https://calscape.org/storage/app/media/qr/Wyethia-mollis-%28Mule-Ears%29.png');
